@id n2_thomas
# DRAFT
# Thomas at dusk, at his herbs in the infirmary (night 2). He opens, quietly, with the prior about the abbey at night
# (n2_thomas_prior): true, and the prior is innocent. Then the merchant: drowned drunk (his lie), or alive, or turned away.
# The knock with no one there: boys from the lane. Bede's warning about the bread: Bede fasts and sees things.
# Telling him about the bread is the wrong brother (Suspicion +5). Bede is already dead; Thomas knows it.
# Claims: n2_thomas_drowned (lie: no water in the lungs, rope marks on the wrists; confront with merchant_rope).
== start [set n2_thomas_prior]
(Thomas looks past you at the door before he speaks, and keeps his voice low.)
Thomas {grave}: Brother. I've seen the prior about the abbey at night. In the court, by the guesthouse, long after Compline.
Thomas {grave, nod}: He has no business there at that hour. I don't say what it means. Only, if you see a man in the dark, it may be Hugh.
-> merchant [if died_merchant]
-> lived [if n1_merchant=admitted]
-> refused [if n1_merchant=refused]
-> topics

== merchant
-> merchant_thomas [if reported_merchant=thomas]
-> merchant_prior [if reported_merchant=prior]
-> merchant_plain

== merchant_thomas
Thomas {warm, still}: And the merchant. You did right to come to me this morning, and quietly. Ale and a fishpond: no fault of yours.
* [if not read_n2_thomas_drowned] He was sober at my gate, brother. -> n2_thomas_drowned
* (Say nothing.) -> topics

== merchant_prior
Thomas {warm, still}: And the merchant. You took him to Hugh, I hear. He'll have made it your doing. It wasn't. The man was drunk.
* [if not read_n2_thomas_drowned] He was sober at my gate, brother. -> n2_thomas_drowned
* (Say nothing.) -> topics

== merchant_plain
Thomas {warm, still}: And the merchant. Ale, and a fishpond in the dark. It's no fault of yours, brother. Don't carry him.
* [if not read_n2_thomas_drowned] He was sober at my gate, brother. -> n2_thomas_drowned
* (Say nothing.) -> topics

== n2_thomas_drowned [claim n2_thomas_drowned lie]
(He sets the pestle down.)
Thomas {warm, still}: I pressed the pond out of his chest with my own hands, brother. He drowned. Drink and the dark, nothing more.
* [believe] God rest him, then. -> drowned_believed
* [press] A man who stood so steady at my gate? -> drowned_pressed
* [confront merchant_rope] Then who tied his hands? There were rope marks on his wrists. -> drowned_broken

== drowned_believed
Thomas {warm, nod}: God rest him. Say his name at Matins, if you like. It does the living good.
-> topics

== drowned_pressed
Thomas {warm, still}: Steady men drink too, brother. I've laid out enough of them to know.
(He takes up the pestle again.)
-> topics

== drowned_broken
(The pestle stops. For a moment his face is a stranger's.)
Thomas {cold, still}: Rope marks.
Thomas {warm}: They drew him out with a rope, brother, and Dunstan with his boathook. A drowned man's skin marks like wet clay.
Thomas {warm, nod}: You've a sharp eye. Keep it on your gate.
-> topics

== lived
Thomas {amused}: Your merchant left at first light, cursing the porter who locked him in like a sheep. Well. He's alive to curse.
-> topics

== refused
Thomas {grave}: You turned the merchant away. We receive every guest as Christ, the Rule says. Still, it was your first night.
-> topics

== again
(Thomas is back at his mortar.)
Thomas {warm}: Brother. Supper soon.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n2_thomas_why] What would the prior be doing out at night? -> why
* [if n1_knock_no_one] [if not n2_thomas_knock] Last night there was a knock at the gate, and no one there. -> knock
* [if bread_warned] [if not n2_thomas_bread] Someone warned me not to eat the bread. -> bread

== why [set n2_thomas_why]
Thomas {grave}: I don't know, and I'd rather not guess at a brother's sins.
Thomas {warm, nod}: You're up all night. You'll see more than I do. Watch, that's all I ask.
-> topics

== knock [set n2_thomas_knock]
(For a moment he doesn't answer. Then he smiles.)
Thomas {warm}: Boys from the lane, knocking and running. They did it to Anselm for years.
Thomas {warm}: And Mab sleeps more than she lets on. Don't lose sleep over a knock.
-> topics

== bread [set n2_thomas_bread] [suspicion 5]
Thomas {warm}: Bede, was it? I saw him at your ear.
Thomas {warm, still}: Bede fasts till he faints, and then he sees things in the rafters. Eat your bread, brother. You need your strength.
-> topics

== leave
Thomas {grave}: Keep it between us, brother. About the prior.
